From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: RtlGetCurrentProcessorNumberEx without a FIXME per call

RtlGetCurrentProcessorNumberEx answered correctly for the one processor group the system reports (group 0, the current processor), but wrote a semi-stub FIXME line on every call; Qt programs (Anki, Audacity, Blender, LibreOffice, MuseScore, Telegram and more import it) call it often, so their logs filled with it. It is a TRACE now.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c
@@ -1980,7 +1980,13 @@
  */
 void WINAPI RtlGetCurrentProcessorNumberEx(PROCESSOR_NUMBER *processor)
 {
+    /* (wine-sg 8262) the system has one processor group (SystemLogicalProcessorInformationEx says so), so
+     * the group is 0 and the number the processor's own; no FIXME per call (Qt programs ask often) */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_PROCNUMEX_FIXME
     FIXME("(%p) :semi-stub\n", processor);
+#else
+    TRACE("(%p)\n", processor);
+#endif
     processor->Group = 0;
     processor->Number = NtGetCurrentProcessorNumber();
     processor->Reserved = 0;
